  ### Additional Block 
    This block is created by BRIC not in the list of BehaviorCapability in DB.
    Options for each parameter are in the DB.
    Show the string defined 'display name' part, and send it 
    - move_to_pose
      blockInfo:
        action: 'BRIC:move_to_pose'
        category: "Navigation"
        description: "Select area / floor / session / POI"
        enabled: true
        parameters[]: 4 cascading dropdowns
          - area:
            options[]: unique area values from AreaInformation.area column
                       FULL string from DB is used as both value and display_name (e.g. "LG sciencepark W02")
          - floor: JSON keys from AreaInformation.information column (e.g. "1", "2", "M", "B1")
            options[]: unique floor according to the selected area.
                       each option carries 'area' metadata for cascading
          - session: JSON array values for each floor in AreaInformation.information
              e.g. information = {"1": ["default", "elevator_AB"], ...}
            options[]: unique session according to the selected area and floor.
                       each option carries 'area' and 'floor' metadata for cascading
          - poi: unique POI values from POI table filtered by the selected area and floor.
            options[]: only POIs with all three coordinates (position_x/y/z) included
                       value = POI.name; display_name = disambiguated label (area › name when duplicate)
                       each option carries 'area', 'floor', 'position_x/y/z' metadata
                       descriptions: POI.description from DB
      Block UI rules (generator_engine.py):
        - Block title label: action_label = X after stripping "BRIC:" prefix → "move_to_pose"
          Rule: for any "BRIC:X" or "BRIC.Y:Z" action, action_label is the last path segment after ":"
        - Param labels: shown for all params (output_name != action_label);
          suppressed only when output_name == action_label (e.g. legacy BRIC:area case)
        - Dropdown option deduplication: static dropdown definitions require unique values
          (Blockly FieldDropdown rejects duplicate values — causes field creation failure and
           breaks setHoverOptionHelp setup). In generator_engine.py, dd list is deduplicated
           by value before appending to args0. The full option_descriptions map (keyed by both
           value and display_name) is still built from ALL options for help popup lookup.
        - Help popup for POI options: indexed by value ("Rack") AND display_name
          ("LG sciencepark W02 › Hanging Rack") so lookup succeeds regardless of whether
          Blockly provides data-value or falls back to textContent.
      Implementation (db_sync.py):
        _fetch_area_information_rows(client):
          SELECT area, information FROM AreaInformation
          → parses information JSON → returns [{area, information: {floor: [sessions]}}]
        _fetch_poi_rows(client):
          SELECT name, display_name, area, floor, position_x, position_y, position_z, description FROM POI
        _BRIC_MOVE_TO_POSE_TEMPLATE: seeded with placeholder options to force dropdown generation
        _ensure_bric_move_to_pose_block(path): inserts block before other BRIC blocks if absent
        _update_move_to_pose_block_options(path, area_info_rows, poi_rows):
          Builds and writes area/floor/session/poi options into the block entry in BlockListRobot.json.
          area opts:    [{value: area, display_name: area}] — FULL string from DB column
          floor opts:   unique (area, floor) pairs; each carries 'area' metadata
          session opts: unique (area, floor, session) triples; each carries 'area' and 'floor' metadata
          poi opts:     only rows with all 3 coords; carry area, floor, position_x/y/z, description
        _write_bric_move_to_pose_ref(path, poi_rows):
          Writes btInfo/bric_move_to_pose.json — maps composite key to pose data.
          Only POIs with all three coordinates are included.
          Key format: "{area}::{floor}::{poi_name}"  (3-part composite for uniqueness)
          Format: [{"name": "{area}::{floor}::{poi_name}",
                    "data": {"pose_type": "map", "pose": {"x": ..., "y": ..., "z": ...}}}]
        _remove_old_bric_blocks(path):
          Removes any deprecated BRIC:area and BRIC.POI:navigation/move_to_pose entries
        Sync call order in sync_block_info_from_db:
          1. _ensure_bric_move_to_pose_block   → insert block if absent
          2. _update_move_to_pose_block_options → populate options
          3. _remove_old_bric_blocks            → remove deprecated entries
          4. _write_bric_move_to_pose_ref       → write bric_move_to_pose.json
      Cascading JS (generator_engine.py emit_block_file):
        Detects 'BRIC:move_to_pose' block and emits an IIFE inside registerBlocks_<module>().
        Builds:
          sessTree = {area: {floor: [[display, value], ...]}} from session raw_options
          poiTree  = {area: {floor: [[display, value], ...]}} from poi raw_options
        4-field cascade:
          areaField.setValidator → rebuilds floor, session, poi dropdowns for new area
          floorField.setValidator → rebuilds session, poi dropdowns for new floor
          Init: sets menuGenerator_ for floor, session, poi using default area value
      Export (two paths, both must produce the same result):
        JS path (generator_engine.py emit_generator_file):
          Builds POI_COORDS = {"area::floor::poi_name": {x, y, z}} from poi raw_options.
          Custom forBlock for 'BRIC:move_to_pose':
            reads PARAM_AREA, PARAM_FLOOR, PARAM_POI field values
            looks up coordKey = "{area}::{floor}::{poi}" in POI_COORDS
            emits navigation/move_to_pose BT node with pose coords
        Python path (app.py preprocess_export_tree → walk()):
          Detects action == "BRIC:move_to_pose" (before BRIC_ACTION_RE check).
          Reads area, floor, poi from node["parameter"] dict.
          Builds composite key: "{area}::{floor}::{poi}"
          Calls load_ref("bric_move_to_pose") to get {key → data} dict.
          Replaces node["action"] with "navigation/move_to_pose"
          Replaces node["parameter"] with matched pose data from bric_move_to_pose.json.
          Error added to resolution_errors if key not found.
      BT export format:
        {
          "type": "Action",
          "action": "navigation/move_to_pose",
          "parameter": {
            "pose_type": "map",
            "pose": {
              "x": {position_x},
              "y": {position_y},
              "z": {position_z}
            }
          }
        }

## Help popup for option descriptions

  ### Overview
    Each block parameter dropdown can show a help popup when the user hovers over
    an option item in the open dropdown. The description is sourced from the
    `description` field of each option entry in BlockListRobot.json parameters.

  ### option_descriptions indexing (generator_engine.py)
    The generated JS constant OPTION_PARAM_MAP stores option_descriptions for each
    parameter. These are used by the setHoverOptionHelp() function at runtime.

    option_descriptions is indexed by BOTH the raw `value` AND the `display_name`
    of each option:
      { "double_nod": "머리 두번...", "nod twice": "머리 두번..." }

    Reason: Blockly dropdown menu items may not carry a `data-value` attribute,
    so the runtime valueFromMenuItem() function may fall back to reading textContent,
    which returns the display name rather than the raw value. Indexing by both
    ensures the lookup succeeds regardless of which form Blockly provides.

    This applies to:
    - Top-level parameter options (build_behavior_block in generator_engine.py)
    - Nested option-parameter options (build_nested_param_meta in generator_engine.py)

  ### Block-level tooltip (setTooltip)
    Blockly's native tooltip (set via this.setTooltip()) must be cleared to empty string.
    Block descriptions are shown ONLY through the HELP icon click popup (setClickHelp).
    Reason: if setTooltip(tip) is set, Blockly shows the native tooltip on hover over any
    block body — including blocks on other rows — causing the wrong block's description to
    appear behind or alongside the custom popup for a different block.
    Rule: always call this.setTooltip('') in the wrappedInit function in generator_engine.py.

  ### Hover trigger
    - Hovering the closed dropdown field: shows description of the currently selected option.
    - Hovering items inside the open dropdown: shows description of the item under cursor.
    - The active field is tracked via window.BRIC.activeOptionHelpField so the correct
      option_descriptions map is used when multiple dropdowns exist on the same block.

## Reference files (btInfo/)

  ### start_motion.json
    Written by _update_start_motion_json() in db_sync.py.
    Each entry uses display_name for the human-readable `name` key and raw DB name in `data`:
      { "name": "expressive_motion.{display_name}", "data": { "task_type": "expressive_motion", "name": "{name}", "repeat": 0 } }
    This keeps the UI label human-friendly while BT generation uses the raw value.
    Loaded by load_ref("start_motion") in app.py walk() for BRIC.start_motion:motion/start_motion export.

  ### bric_move_to_pose.json
    Written by _write_bric_move_to_pose_ref() in db_sync.py.
    Each entry maps a composite key "{area}::{floor}::{poi_name}" to pose data:
      { "name": "{area}::{floor}::{poi_name}", "data": { "pose_type": "map", "pose": { "x": ..., "y": ..., "z": ... } } }
    Only POIs with all three coordinates (position_x, position_y, position_z) are included.
    Loaded by load_ref("bric_move_to_pose") in app.py walk() for BRIC:move_to_pose export.
    Composite key used for lookup: "{area}::{floor}::{poi}" where values come from block fields.
